# plan: PLAN-X01-v5.1 sha256 af4fee6b847caca46afd2456818d510e817cb09699b91034270ac7f4a6a75393 (IV-signed; this stub cites it)
# task: script 3: A1 known-answer test: 8 rows on 135 gate books (3 sets x G1,G2,NULL x 15); writes runs/vx01_a1/a1_scores.csv and results_vx01_a1.txt. GATE NOT RUN.
# note: dev log vx01_a1_known_answer_dev_runs.log is hash-chained; its SHA256 at freeze is dev_log_sha256; gate log vx01_a1_known_answer_gate_runs.log is not in the stub
# note: secondary report-only small-inventory books NOT implemented: plan gives no seeds and no suffix count (open question)
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 66): 2. **Gate math, 9 cells (checked by IV).** A gate needs >=10/15 folds (or books) in each of 9 cells (3 transliterations x 3 gate seeds). One cell: p=0.733 per fold clears 81.2%, p=0.8 clears 93.9%. Nine cells if independent: p=0.733 -> 15%; p=0.8 -> 57%; p=0.84 -> 81%; 80% needs p ~0.837. Folds, seeds and transliterations share data, so real odds are lower. **Strictness is intended:** a failed gate costs coverage (UNINFORMATIVE), never a false call. An "at most 4/15 in all 9 cells" control: per-fold match 0.1 -> passes 89.1%; 0.2 -> 19.9% (both recomputed).
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 70): 6. **Thresholds.** F1 >=0.85, exact triple >=0.70, null false-structure <=5%, >=10/15 are ARBITRARY BUT FIXED before any run, confirmed by Eve 2026-10-18 22:17 PDT, not tuned on data. Link to A2: F1 0.85 allows about 15% boundary error, so A2 injects error at the measured e and at 1.5 x e. The 10/15 gate is the project's D-068 rule.
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 71): 7. A flip under a segmenter counts as evidence only if that segmenter is ADEQUATE ON PLANTED BOOKS (A1).
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 98): **A1 known-answer test.** Hypothesis: a segmenter recovers planted prefix/core/suffix.
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 99): - *Freeze order.* (0) Freeze `vx01_common.py` (seed guard, logger, stub check) first. (1) Freeze `vx01_seg_mdl.py` + stub BEFORE any A1 book exists (dev books included); never tuned on A1 books. (2) Write `vx01_a1_gen.py` + `vx01_a1_metrics.py` (own generators, no SlotSegmenter import, a (prefix, core, suffix) triple saved per token). (3) Dev books only for the oracle ceiling. (4) Freeze gen, metrics, thresholds, gate seeds, dev-log hash. (5) Generate gate books, score. Existing segmenters (Slot, Zattera, Seg_Affix2, Canonical) imported unchanged.
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 100): - *Inventory sizes are FIXED numbers (IV 5a), not measured by a segmenter under test.* They are Slot's own outputs on real text, used only as sizes: tokens per book 34,857 / 34,618 / 34,411 (`results_s76.txt:34,37,40`); prefixes (incl. empty) 28 / 29 / 25 and cores 2,360 / 2,491 / 2,420 (`results_s76.txt:48,53,58`); suffixes (incl. empty) 19 / 20 / 20 (`results_s34_morphology_syntax_geography.txt:11,208,376`; those runs use slightly different counts, 29/2,335 etc., so the numbers are approximate sizes only). These three sets are ZL3b-, RF1b-, IT2a-sized. **G1 results are labelled "at Slot-sized inventories" and favour Slot; G1 is not a test on a Slot-independent inventory. G2 is Rugg-sized (250 rows, columns 40/60/40, `ctl_generators.py:77, 95`), not Slot-sized. NULL is matched to the real transliteration marginals.** Report-only secondary books at a small, Zattera-sized inventory (25 prefixes, 163 cores, `results_s76.txt:49`) are scored but do not gate.
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 101): - *Books (per transliteration set, 15 gate books each).* **G1:** independent prefix x core x suffix draws, Zipf exponent 1.0 (arbitrary, fixed), pieces drawn from the frozen EVA glyph list by vx01 code. **G2 (Rugg-like, IV 5b):** a table-and-grille LIKE `ctl_generators.py:77-113` (rows 250, columns of 40/60/40 pieces, 40 grilles; word = column 0 + 1 + 2, :105); **each of the 15 books has its own table seed and its own grille seed** (3a); true labels = the three column picks; Rugg-sized inventories. Pieces come from fixed glyph pools, not from Voynich text. **NULL (IV 5c):** same token count, same token-frequency (rank-frequency/Zipf) profile as the real transliteration, same glyph unigram rates, same word-length distribution, same lines/page and words/line layout; each word type is an i.i.d. glyph string; NO affix inventory. 3 x 45 = 135 gate books. Note: `ctl_generators.py:77-80` builds its pieces from Voynich words via `split3` (2-glyph ends); vx01 G2 is "like" it only in table/grille shape, because vx01 uses fixed glyph pools.
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 102): - *Metrics, token-weighted, per book.* Truth per token = (P, C, S); internal boundaries = glyph positions len(P) (if P non-empty) and len(P)+len(C) (if S non-empty). **Boundary F1:** micro-average over every token occurrence (token-weighted), exact position (0-glyph tolerance), precision and recall pooled, F1 of the pooled values. **Exact triple rate:** share of tokens with predicted (P, C, S) equal to truth. **False structure (NULL only):** share of tokens given a non-empty prefix OR suffix, per book. Type-weighted F1 reported, not gating. A token a segmenter drops (Zattera) counts as a miss.
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 103): - *Oracle ceiling (dev books).* A dictionary parse knowing the true inventories must reach the thresholds on G1 and G2; otherwise the generator is redesigned on dev seeds before step 4 (code revision, rule 4).
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 104): - *Roll-up.* Book = unit. A segmenter is ADEQUATE ON PLANTED BOOKS only if, in ALL 9 cells (3 sets x {G1, G2, NULL}), >=10 of 15 books pass: G1/G2 book passes if F1 >=0.85 AND exact >=0.70; NULL book passes if false structure <=5%. Strict by design; Slot may fail NULL (any glyph starting >=1% of tokens with high next-glyph entropy becomes a prefix).
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 105): - *Rows scored.* Slot; Zattera primary (drops unparsable tokens: a miss); **Zattera-hybrid** (`Z_S1_whole`: Zattera parse, whole-word core for unparsable tokens); Zattera S2; Seg_Affix2; Canonical; `vx01_seg_mdl.py`; unsegmented words. Zattera-hybrid is scored as its own row because Part B depends on it (section 5).
# decision_rule (verbatim PLAN-X01-v5.1 line 106): - *Outcome label.* "ADEQUATE ON PLANTED BOOKS (G1 at Slot-sized inventories, G2 Rugg-sized)": works only on synthetic books with independent affix draws (Slot's own assumption). It does NOT mean adequate for the Voynich text and does NOT discharge X-01. If NO segmenter, Slot included, is ADEQUATE: X-01 stays at-risk, no finding is upgraded or downgraded, A2/A3 flips are descriptive only, filed as "no segmenter validated".
# threshold_rule: all thresholds exactly as written in the plan lines above; none is changed here.
